{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>There was no fear</b> — like him, like 'this people was no people like him.'" "<b>And the word חונך</b> — from the root חנה, and the kaf is for the second person. Or it is the Messiah, and because the word is from the stative verbs, therefore its meaning is 'those who encamp against you.'" "<b>And the word חונך</b> — it comes in the manner of: 'when He hears, He will answer you.' And the tav of the boshet is for the second person. David put them to shame, for Elohim rejected them."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 53, :notes {2 "Reading פירוש as 'its meaning.' The phrase כשמעתו ענך is ambiguous; translated hyper-literally. The antecedent of 'the tav of the boshet' is uncertain but likely refers to a morphological feature of the suffix in חונך."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:45.039570334Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}